{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Controlling the Story", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Doing Some Research ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about people's  interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important  and specific  information and   aspects in   conversations, texts or   presentations about  the communicative   functions related to  this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important  and specific  information and   aspects in   conversations, texts or   presentations about  the communicative   functions related to  this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important  and specific  information and   aspects in   conversations, texts or   presentations about  the communicative   functions related to  this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important  and specific  information and   aspects in   conversations, texts or   presentations about  the communicative   functions related to  this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important  and specific  information and   aspects in   conversations, texts or   presentations about  the communicative   functions related to  this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important  and specific  information and   aspects in   conversations, texts or   presentations about  the communicative   functions related to  this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important  and specific  information and   aspects in   conversations, texts or   presentations about  the communicative   functions related to  this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important  and specific  information and   aspects in   conversations, texts or   presentations about  the communicative   functions related to  this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Organizing Points in an Argument", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are many ways to organize points in an argument. One clear method is to use ordinal numbers (<span class=\"italic\">first, second, third ... </span>).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "An ordinal number may be the subject of your sentence if you  can state the topic of your point as a noun.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Example: First is listening. It is useless to present an argument if you do not know the other person's position.  </br>Second is clarification. You must be certain you completely understand.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An ordinal number may also be followed by a comma, before  the main clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">First, I want you to listen to this recording. </br>Second, please make notes every time you find an error.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Using ordinal  numbers as the   subject of your   sentence for each  main point\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Using ordinal  numbers to   introduce the main   clause explaining   your point\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">First is ... </br> Second is ...  </br>Third is ...  </br>Fourth is ...</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">First, </br> Second, </br> Third, </br> Fourth,</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "First method: </br><span class=\"italic\">Politics is like a game.<ul><li><span class=\"underline\">First are</span> the teams.<li><span class=\"underline\">Second are</span> the fans.<li><span class=\"underline\">Third are</span> the people who don't care at all.<li><span class=\"underline\">Fourth is</span> the competition.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Second method:</br><span class=\"italic\">Politics is like a game.<ul><li><span class=\"underline\">First,</span> there are teams. The members are chosen according to their abilities.<li><span class=\"underline\">Second,</span> you have fans. People choose which side  they prefer and they put a lot of energy into   supporting their team.<li><span class=\"underline\">Third,</span>  you have people who don't care at all. They  don't think the game (or politics) is relevant to their  lives.<li><span class=\"underline\">Fourth,</span> you have competition.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Using the <span class=\"italic\">Present Passive</span> When Solving a Problem", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present Passive tense</span> is used when an action is  performed on another object (person or thing) in the present.   Put the object at the beginning of the clause. Then use the  verb 'to be' in the present tense, followed by the past participle of your verb.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here are some situations that are stated in the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present tense</span> using the<span class=\"strong\"> Active Form</span>. The problem solving steps are stated in the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present tense</span> using the<span class=\"strong\"> Passive Form</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Situation 1 (Present Tense: Active Form)<ul><li><span class=\"underline\">Imagine </span>(active)<span class=\"underline\">a herd of cows that have worms</span>  (object).</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Problem Solving Steps (Present Tense: Passive Form) <ol><li>First, the animals <span class=\"underline\">are given</span> medicine. (Present Passive)<li>Second, the animals <span class=\"underline\">are carefully watched.</span> (Present Passive)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Situation 2 (Present Tense: Active Form)<ul><li>Now imagine a <span class=\"underline\">business </span>(object) that has problems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Problem Solving Steps (Present Tense: Passive Form)<ol><li>The business deal <span class=\"underline\">is offered</span>. (Present Passive)<li>The business deal <span class=\"underline\">is observed</span>. (Present Passive)</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Situation</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Using  Present   Tense in   Active Form   to Describe   Problem   Solving   Steps</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Using the  Present   Passive to   Describe the   Steps</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A man has a  vision  problem.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The man  looks for   someone to   give him a   doctor's  appointment.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The man <span class=\\\"italic\\\">is   given</span> a   doctor's   appointment.\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The doctor  refers  the man to a specialist.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The man <span class=\\\"italic\\\">is  referred</span> to a   specialist by   his doctor.\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The specialist  examines the  man's vision.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The man <span class=\\\"italic\\\">is  examined   by</span> by the   specialist.\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The specialist  orders a  prescription  for glasses.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The man<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> is  ordered</span> a   prescription   for glasses   by the   specialist.\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The glasses  correct the   man's vision.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The man's   vision<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> is   corrected </span>by   the glasses.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Notice how the man remains the subject of attention no  matter what other things happen. The present passive voice is very useful to keep attention on your subject if you have multiple steps to introduce.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at some examples of the Present Passive in a <span class=\"underline\">question form</span>: <br> Examples: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Can these issues be resolved quickly? <br>What is the first thing that should be done?<br> How many people can be added to the meeting list? <br> How are crises prevented by business owners?</span> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stage", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a level or step in a process", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are four main stages of crisis management.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use at work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "symptom", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sign of a problem that is felt or seen;  usually refers to illness", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This is similar to the early symptoms of an illness.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to identify", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to recognize and know exactly what  someone or something is", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The problem is now identified, like an illness which  is recognized.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ongoing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "continuing without a known end", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Third is the Ongoing Crisis Stage.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "result", "type": "name"}, {"content": "final effect; consequence", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The results of the problem are seen clearly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "discouragement", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the feeling that efforts are useless", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This is the stage of discouragement because solving the problem takes time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "resolution", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the stage where the solution to a problem has completely worked", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fourth is the Crisis Resolution Stage.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to resolve", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to fix or solve a problem", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Although the crisis is resolved, careful watch is still important.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine a job situation that needs several steps of planning to complete.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down the steps that need to be done. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Order the steps.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your plan of action to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I create a plan of action in a work situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe steps that need to be taken.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I order the steps to a plan of action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my plan of action to my partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about jobs and work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can organize points in an argument.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can solve problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "How often have you experienced a crisis in the  workplace?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "  Who is responsible for dealing with crises at work?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"cont